\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Determine the classes of varieties $X/k$ for which the canonical map $X(k)\to\Gamma^{\mathrm{et}}(X/k)$ is a bijection, where $\Gamma^{\mathrm{et}}(X/k)$ is the set of homotopy classes of sections of the étale-homotopy fibration $\Pi^{\mathrm{et}}(X)\to\Pi^{\mathrm{et}}(k)$.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2024/45}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Determine the classes of varieties $X/k$ for which the canonical map $X(k)\to\Gamma^{\mathrm{et}}(X/k)$ is a bijection, where $\Gamma^{\mathrm{et}}(X/k)$ is the set of homotopy classes of sections of the étale-homotopy fibration $\Pi^{\mathrm{et}}(X)\to\Pi^{\mathrm{et}}(k)$.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30006070 (OWR-14298795-005). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2024/45}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30006070}

